# nr-tui-view: the application view of mixdog-tui (native/core/crates/mixdog-tui): src/view.rs, src/view/{bands,chrome,format,hint,labels,panel,prompt,rows,spinner,welcome}.rs,
# tests/app_view_twin.rs, tests/cases/app_view.json, tests/goldens/app_view.json, tests/recorders/{record-app-view,gen-app-view-cases}.mjs
# Nothing here could be compiled (no cargo in this task).

## 1. Cargo, workspace, protocol: no change
mixdog-tui already depends on every crate the view uses (mixdog-term, mixdog-termtext, mixdog-tui-style, mixdog-tui-widgets, mixdog-js,
mixdog-view-model, serde_json); lib.rs already declares `pub mod view;`. No Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, workspace member, protocol row or
compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING entry is needed.

## 2. What nr-tui-app (the application state and the run loop) must apply
Per frame, in this order (all of it is in mixdog_tui::view):
 1. `surface::layout::compute_shell_layout` -> ShellLayout (the view reads it whole).
 2. Items: `transcript::window` (row index, render window), `visible_items::overlay_hint_placement` over the mounted items, then
    `view::rows::mount_rows(&mut ItemHeights, &MountInput { .. })` -> MountedRows. `now_ms` is the wall clock (tool cards blink and count from it).
 3. An open picker: `view::panel::fit_picker(&mut props, frame_columns, &layout)` (columns, visible rows, fill height are the view's decision,
    not the picker's).
 4. The spinner row: `view::spinner::spinner_props(&SpinnerContext { .. })` -> `mixdog_tui_widgets::spinner::render_spinner(&mut SpinnerProgress, ..)`;
    the SpinnerProgress lives in the application state (one per live spinner), the clock is read by the run loop.
 5. The statusline text is the footer's current line (`footer::StatuslineText`), the workflow is `state.workflow`.
 6. `view::render_app(&AppViewProps { .. }, &mut Painter::new(&mut grid))` over a grid of the terminal's columns x rows (the frame is one column
    narrower). The returned AppFrame carries the hardware cursor (`cursor`, pass it to FrameWriter::write_frame / PacedFrames::draw), the content
    box of the prompt (`prompt_box`: call `PromptEditor::cursor_anchor(&box, enabled)` with it so the editor publishes the box rect for the
    mouse handler and the caret of the next key), and what the floating panel took (`panel`).
Stateful parts the run loop owns and steps:
 - `view::chrome::TerminalChrome`: resize events (`on_resize_event(now)`, then `update(columns, rows)` when it returns true; `poll(now)` at
   `next_due()`), the extended-keys write once at the mount (`extended_keys_once(raw_mode_supported, &ModeEnv)`), and the input gate
   (`tick_after_mount()` one loop pass after the first frame, `is_ready()` into AppViewProps::tui_ready).
 - `view::hint::WelcomePromptHint`: `refresh(&mut dyn WelcomeProbes, &HintInputs)` whenever provider, model, workflow id or the error toast
   signature may have changed (it skips unchanged inputs itself; `invalidate()` when the store is replaced), `dismiss(refs.welcome_prompt_hint_visible)`
   when the draft gains its first character. The WelcomeProbes impl forwards `getProviderSetup`, `listProviderModels({quick:true})`,
   `listWorkflows`, `getWebSearchRoute` to the store and answers None for a method the store does not have.
 - Boot: `view::welcome::boot_splash(columns, windows_like_terminal(env), cwd, version, styler)` is written to the alternate screen before the
   first frame (then the first frame overprints it); `version` is the crate version of the binary.
 - The slash palette: `view::step_palette_index(index, PaletteMove::parse(direction), total)` for the editor's onCommandPaletteNavigate.
The Node recording needs C:/Project/mixdog (node_modules for esbuild, ink, react): `node tests/recorders/record-app-view.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog
--cases tests/cases/app_view.json --check tests/goldens/app_view.json` (cases are generated by tests/recorders/gen-app-view-cases.mjs).
The plan's verify line names record-ink-frames.mjs for this file; that recorder is the widgets crate's and has no component for a whole screen, so
the screens use record-app-view.mjs (same esbuild + Ink method, plus the hardware cursor read from the Ink instance).

## 3. Panel decisions the view defines but the key handlers apply
 - Tool approval: `view::panel::approval_key_decision(input)` is the approval picker's onKey (a/y approve, d/n deny); a selected row is
   `ToolDecision::decide(value == "approve")`, Escape `ToolDecision::decide(false)`; a submitted question is `ToolDecision::answered(answers)`,
   a dismissed one `ToolDecision::dismissed()`. `ToolDecision::to_value()` is the decision object of the store's resolveToolApproval(id, decision).
 - A picker without an owner cancel handler closes through the surface claim (`claim().close()`) and clears the prompt hint; a picker selection
   goes through `surface::latch` (the Enter latch). Both are the panel handlers' job (nr-tui-handlers / nr-tui-app), as in floating-panel.jsx.
